  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "The only completed experiment (config_001) establishes that RNA-only with PCA and a single profile yields ~0.485 accuracy, giving us a reference for the RNA signal. The largest remaining uncertainty is whether the image modality carries any discriminative signal at all. If image contributes nothing, then all 36 multimodal configurations become low-priority, dramatically reshaping the search. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is a clean, single-variable test: it isolates the image signal using a standard, well-understood encoder (ResNet-50) while keeping the profile setting minimal. This is the highest-information next experiment because the answer (image helps vs. doesn't) determines whether the multimodal branch of the design space is worth further budget, and it avoids confounding the image effect with multiprofile aggregation or fusion choices."
}

